// us.irs.pub_15t_2026 — IRS Publication 15-T (2026): Federal Income Tax
// Withholding Methods.
//
// WHY A PACKAGE. Ten coverage rows (employment.json: 26/3402/b/u1–u4 —
// percentage method; 26/3402/c/u1–u6 — wage bracket) require the tax
// «determined in accordance with tables prescribed by the Secretary»;
// the bridge regulations §31.3402(b)-1(a) and (c)-1(a)(2) (pinned in
// `us.cfr.t26_31_3402_b_c_h_m`) name those tables as the «applicable ...
// tables ... set forth in the applicable forms, instructions, publications
// ... prescribed by the Commissioner» — i.e. this publication. Section 6
// additionally mirrors the four §3402(h) alternative methods for the
// sixteen rows 26/3402/h/*. No row names a concrete edition: owners need
// the annual-issue contract «For use in 2026», not the archive.
//
// WHAT IT HOLDS (phase 1, still rule-less). `sources/p15t-2026.pdf` —
// the official IRS bytes (2,480,887 bytes, 71 pages, Catalog 32112B),
// pinned by sha256 (`sources/provenance.json`: URL, bytes, sha256,
// last-modified, edition, section inventory — no table values). Seven
// sections: 1 (percentage, automated), 2–3 (wage bracket, by W-4 vintage),
// 4–5 (percentage, manual, by W-4 vintage), 6 (alternative methods),
// 7 (Indian gaming — out of the 33-row scope).
// `sources/tables/*.lawtable.json` (6 tables, 450 rows, `total: false`:
// annual + manual-2020 + manual-2019 percentage schedules, Tables 3–6
// periods, Table 7 allowances, §6 tolerances) + `sources.law`
// (63 quote-anchored fragments) + `edition-index.json` — all GENERATED by
// `corpus/tools/sources/sync/sync_us_irs_pub15t.py --emit-derived` from
// the pinned PDF, never hand-edited; `--check` re-parses and byte-compares
// (drift 0). Wage-bracket cells (§§2/3) and §7 tables are out of phase 1
// (recon item; edition-index unresolved). No rules: the value, its table
// and its reading belong to the owner, the figures entering the case as
// case facts. Same shape as `us.irs.rev_rul_afr` (phase 1).
//
// LAYOUT NOTE. `check_laws_tree` §3.5 derives `us/pub-15t-2026` from
// jurisdiction US + instrument guidance (`us.irs` is not a
// GROUP_BY_NAME_PREFIX group): the package name keeps the `irs` issuer
// segment, the path does not — same as `us/rev-rul-afr`.
//
// OUT OF SCOPE. Prior-year editions (URL template `irs-prior/p15t--YYYY`);
// wage-bracket cell tables §§2–3 in phase 1 (deferred: thousands of cells
// under 6-column interleave — recon item, see README); §7 gaming tables
// (§3402(r) rows are EXECUTABLE); anything beyond «For use in 2026».

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irs.pub_15t_2026 version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irs:pub_15t_2026:clir";
